// =============================================================================
// BND-2186 - Backfill of loadDate on the Data Vault fiscal-code satellite
// =============================================================================
//
// Context (agreed solution - "SOLUZIONE 1", parametric time window)
//   The incremental pipeline `idpay_data_vault_copy` extracts from Cosmos only
//   the records whose technical source field `createdAt` falls in a UTC
//   half-open window [fromDate, toDate) and appends the new fiscal codes to
//   `data_vault` (join kind=leftanti on `_id`), stamping loadDate = now().
//   `createdAt` is used ONLY as a source-side filter: it is NOT copied into ADX,
//   so there is nothing to refill for it. `updateDate` has been dropped (records
//   are immutable and never updated).
//
// When is this needed?
//   Only as a SAFETY NET for the one-off INITIAL FULL LOAD of the historical
//   content, IF that load is performed with a raw copy that bypasses the append
//   step (which otherwise sets loadDate = now()). In that case historical rows
//   land with loadDate = NULL and this script stamps them once.
//   If the initial full load goes through the normal append path, loadDate is
//   already set and this script is a no-op.
//
// Execution
//   Run MANUALLY, at most once, against the `idpay` database, AFTER the initial
//   full load and BEFORE enabling the daily window-based run. Idempotent: rows
//   that already have loadDate are left untouched (coalesce).
//
// Notes
//   - Adjust `backfill_ts` to the agreed historical/migration timestamp.
//   - The fiscal code lives in column `data` (PII): it is never projected to
//     logs here, only `_id`, `page` and `loadDate` are rewritten.
// =============================================================================

.set-or-replace data_vault <|
let backfill_ts = datetime(2026-10-23T00:00:00Z);
data_vault
| extend loadDate = coalesce(loadDate, backfill_ts)
| project _id, data, page, loadDate

